  { "name": "pwrite",  "wave": "x1.0.x.." },
  { "name": "paddr",   "wave": "x=.=.x..", "data": ["0x0", "0x0"] },
  { "name": "pwdata",  "wave": "x=.x....", "data": ["D0"] },
  { "name": "pready",  "wave": "1......." },
  { "name": "prdata",  "wave": "x...=x..", "data": ["D0"] }
],
  "head": { "text": "write DATA (push) then read DATA (pop), zero wait states" } }
```

### Code
```systemverilog
module apb_fifo #(
  parameter  int DW    = 32,
  parameter  int DEPTH = 8,                  // power of two for wrap-bit pointers
  localparam int AW    = $clog2(DEPTH)
) (
  input  logic          pclk, presetn,
  input  logic          psel, penable, pwrite,
  input  logic [3:0]    paddr,
  input  logic [DW-1:0] pwdata,
  output logic [DW-1:0] prdata,
  output logic          pready, pslverr
);
  logic [DW-1:0] mem [DEPTH];
  logic [AW:0]   wptr, rptr;                 // extra MSB distinguishes full/empty
  logic          full, empty;
  logic [AW:0]   count;

  assign count = wptr - rptr;
  assign empty = (wptr == rptr);
  assign full  = (wptr[AW] != rptr[AW]) && (wptr[AW-1:0] == rptr[AW-1:0]);

  wire access   = psel && penable;           // pready is always 1 → completion
  wire sel_data = (paddr[3:2] == 2'd0);
  wire sel_stat = (paddr[3:2] == 2'd1);
  wire do_push  = access &&  pwrite && sel_data && !full;
  wire do_pop   = access && !pwrite && sel_data && !empty;

  assign pready = 1'b1;

  always_comb begin
    prdata  = '0;
    pslverr = 1'b0;
    if (access) begin
      unique case (1'b1)
        sel_data: if (pwrite) pslverr = full;
                  else begin
                    pslverr = empty;
                    prdata  = empty ? '0 : mem[rptr[AW-1:0]];
                  end
        sel_stat: if (pwrite) pslverr = 1'b1;     // read-only register
                  else prdata = DW'({count, full, empty});
        default:  pslverr = 1'b1;                 // unmapped address
      endcase
    end
  end

  always_ff @(posedge pclk) if (do_push) mem[wptr[AW-1:0]] <= pwdata;

  always_ff @(posedge pclk or negedge presetn)
    if (!presetn) begin
      wptr <= '0; rptr <= '0;
    end else begin
      if (do_push) wptr <= wptr + 1'b1;
      if (do_pop)  rptr <= rptr + 1'b1;
    end
endmodule
```

### Explanation
- Acting in the setup phase or on every `PSEL` cycle would push/pop twice or on aborted transfers — always qualify with `PENABLE` (and `PREADY` when it can be low).
- **SRAM-based FIFO**: the head isn't available combinationally, so either prefetch the head into an output register, or start the SRAM read in the setup phase and drive `PREADY=0` for the read-latency cycles.
- PRDATA only needs to be valid in the completing cycle; zeroing it otherwise eases debug.

### Corner cases & pitfalls
- `PSTRB` (APB4): partial writes to a FIFO are usually an error — define it.
- Back-to-back transfers (PSEL held high, new setup right after completion) must not double-pop.
- `presetn` mid-transfer; read of STATUS while a push happens in the same cycle (one bus master → cannot happen on one APB).

### Verification
- UVM APB agent + FIFO reference queue; assertions on APB protocol stability; coverage of push-when-full, pop-when-empty, wait states (if added), every register, back-to-back transfers.

tongxin-106:
**Key idea:** Each side keeps an **(A+1)-bit binary pointer** (A = log2 depth, the extra MSB counts wraps) and its **Gray** version. Only the Gray pointer crosses the clock boundary (through a 2-flop synchronizer), because exactly one bit changes per increment — a mis-sampled value is either the old or the new pointer, never garbage. **Empty** (read side): next read Gray == synchronized write Gray. **Full** (write side): next write Gray == synchronized read Gray with its **top two bits inverted**.

### Gray pointers for DEPTH = 4 (A = 2, 3-bit pointers)
| binary | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| gray | 000 | 001 | 011 | 010 | 110 | 111 | 101 | 100 |

- Empty example: `rgray = 011`, `wgray_sync = 011` → equal → empty.
- Full example: 4 writes, 0 reads: `wgray = 110`, `rgray_sync = 000` → invert top two → `110` → equal → full.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  subgraph WCLK["write clock domain"]
    WB["wbin (A+1)"] --> WG["wgray"]
    WG --> FULL["wfull = wgray_next == {~r[A:A-1], r[A-2:0]}"]
  end
  subgraph RCLK["read clock domain"]
    RB["rbin (A+1)"] --> RG["rgray"]
    RG --> EMPTY["rempty = rgray_next == wgray_sync"]
  end
  WG -->|"2-flop sync"| EMPTY
  RG -->|"2-flop sync"| FULL
  WB -->|"waddr A bits"| MEM["dual-port RAM"]
  RB -->|"raddr A bits"| MEM
```

